Jabbim - a Jabber client for mere mortals
=========================================

What is Jabbim
--------------
Jabbim is a user-friendly Jabber (XMPP) client. Its goal is to make the modern
and useful Jabber services approachable to common users. It integrates well
with the advanced functionality provided by the Jabber server of the same name
(see http://www.jabbim.com). Jabbim is written in Python and Qt4.


Requirements
------------
First make sure you have all the dependencies. You need at least:
  - Python 2.5
  - PyQt 4.4 (with QtWebKit support)
  - Twisted (a.k.a. python-twisted; at least -names, -web, -words)
  - pyOpenSSL
  - python-configobj (only needed for running Jabbim installations done with
    'make install')
Optional:
  - Twisted-Web2 (a.k.a. python-twisted-web2) for connecting over HTTP (BOSH).
  - DBus support in PyQt (python-qt4-dbus in Debian, part of PyQt4 in Fedora)
    for the 'tune' plugin in Linux.

How to run Jabbim
-----------------
You can simply run Jabbim directly from the directory, where you have extracted
(or checked out from SVN) the sources, using the command:

  ./jabbim.sh

Most likely that's all you need.


Installation
------------
Most people will not need this, since it's easy to just run Jabbim without
installation. If you really want to install Jabbim into the system for all
users, use:

  make
  make install   (this one as root)

This would install Jabbim by default into the /usr/local hierarchy. If you want
to have it somewhere else, use:

  make PREFIX=/some/path
  make install
